        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "64983851-f0b9-51df-8929-a33b90b9cbad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Game of Life, The Checkered Game of Life, History of the World, Be a Broadway Star\n- People: Milton Bradley, Ragnar Brothers\n- Concepts: Board games, player counts, gameplay mechanics, epochs, empires\n\nFacts:\n- Milton Bradley originally created The Checkered Game of Life in 1860, and the game later became known as The Game of Life or simply Life.\n- The Game of Life has variations that accommodate eight to ten players.\n- Ragnar Brothers designed the board game History of the World, which was originally published in 1991.\n- History of the World is played by up to six players across seven epochs, and each player controls a different empire in each epoch.\n- Be a Broadway Star uses a game board similar to The Game of Life, and players move based on two rolled dice.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ef10bbe7-0b07-57ba-a613-c2328bd16a5b",
        "text": "Page: The Game of Life. Sentence: The Game of Life, also known simply as Life, is a board game originally created in 1860 by Milton Bradley, as The Checkered Game of Life.\nPage: The Game of Life. Sentence: Variations of the game accommodate eight to ten players.\nPage: History of the World (board game). Sentence: History of the World (often abbreviated HotW) is a board game designed by Ragnar Brothers and originally published in 1991.\nPage: History of the World (board game). Sentence: It is played by up to six different players in seven different epochs; each player playing a different empire in each epoch.\nPage: Be a Broadway Star. Sentence: Players move around a game board similar to The Game of Life, with movement determined by two rolled dice.",
